  "articleBody": "Thinking of upgrading your cabinets with D-shaped handles? Great choice! They offer a comfortable grip and a sleek look. But before you start drilling, there are a few important things to consider to ensure a smooth installation. First, always confirm the handle's center-to-center spacing. This is the distance between the two screw holes, and it's absolutely critical for getting your handles to line up. You'll want to either match existing holes or plan your new layout meticulously. Second, think about projection. This refers to how far the handle sticks out from the cabinet. You want enough depth for comfortable finger clearance, especially if you have larger hands. Third, check the screw compatibility. The screws that come with your handles might not always be the perfect length for your cabinet thickness, so be ready to swap them out if needed. Finally, when it comes to D-shaped handles specifically, consider the grip space. Does the curve and depth of the handle feel good in your hand? Test it out! It's all about making your kitchen feel more like home. If you're looking for expert installation or need advice on the best handles for your space in the Denver area, HH Remodeling LLC is always ready to assist.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
